{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/177987-bloodlines-and-blood-ties","id":177987,"title":"Bloodlines and blood ties","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-23T09:10:04-07:00","id":177987,"title":"Bloodlines and blood ties","content":"Does joining a bloodline create blood ties with the Avus and his family?<br /> <br /> Does childe (and other Family members) of of the kindred joining get wired in too?<br /> <br /> Or are their two different circuits so to speak?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T09:59:30-07:00","id":179009,"title":"","content":"Different circuits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T03:03:31-07:00","id":179558,"title":"","content":"There's never been an official rule on it. And, while Griautis is right to the extent that its not talked about in the books, and thus the assuming that nothing changes there... its not unheard of for the individual STs or even writers to have done something along the lines of new Avus = new adoptive sire in individual games.<br /> <br /> Rather than saying that its specifically &quot;different circuits,&quot; I personally am going to say that its going to be an individual ST's call, depending on the needs of the story. Hells, given the nature that some &quot;bloodlines&quot; being more akin to a political path than family, and some firmly in the family vein, it wouldn't be too much of a stretch to see both &quot;new adoption&quot; and &quot;different circuit&quot; in the same game. <br /> <br /> To me, absence of a rule is not a rule of absence - its a blank spot that doesn't necessarily need to be filled in by hard rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T04:46:59-07:00","id":179570,"title":"","content":"It'd be weird depending on the initial relation to the avus. You could join the bloodline at BP 2 if you have a blood tie to them already. To learn it from another clanmate you have no relation to you need BP 4. I wouldn't want to say that the latter avus example suddenly gets 'promoted' to sire level of blood tie; I feel like that diminishes the value of having an avus that you're related to.<br /> <br /> So I'm not sure, but just consider the different types of avus and not rule anything to diminish the value of one type versus another. Or do whatever you feels best is for your game, it's all magic so maybe this instance is unique, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T05:44:02-07:00","id":179588,"title":"","content":"Well, also it creates very strange family trees if you consider that an avus get's connected into the tree. It feels very awkward to connect them, in my opinion. I think, that blood sympathy should always be only related to whom sired you. Mainly taking on the properties of someone else's blood is not enough to create this mystical connection (At least in my book).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T06:20:39-07:00","id":183732,"title":"","content":"Yes the whole new related Avus rules throw a kink in it. I alsp like the adoption mechanic in Strange Dead love. It fits our Style for other reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T09:46:27-07:00","id":183865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/177987-bloodlines-and-blood-ties?p=179588#post179588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, also it creates very strange family trees if you consider that an avus get's connected into the tree. It feels very awkward to connect them, in my opinion. I think, that blood sympathy should always be only related to whom sired you. Mainly taking on the properties of someone else's blood is not enough to create this mystical connection (At least in my book).</div> </div> </div> </div> Bloodlines are defined as &quot;lineages with mutations of the blood.&quot; Seriously, they are - check the glossary in the book. If you join a bloodline, then it follows that you're joining a new lineage. I find that staying tied to your old lineage is more awkward.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T13:52:57-07:00","id":184055,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's also usual for childer to join their sire's bloodline and jumping around in non-family bloodlines is rarer. So that's why the definition holds. They are &quot;lineages&quot;, which may adopt children. Do adopted children count as full children? I wouldn't say so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T14:15:14-07:00","id":184074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/177987-bloodlines-and-blood-ties?p=184055#post184055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do adopted children count as full children? I wouldn't say so.</div> </div> </div> </div> .... Bad phrasing much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T23:40:45-07:00","id":184589,"title":"","content":"Perhaps (not a native speaker), but what I meant is, the usual case for bloodlines, is that a sire gives his bloodline to his childe. That's why they are lineages. That's why this usually is not a problem. Now these BP 4 adopted members.. well they are different and I see no reason for them to have blood ties. (Unless through some elaborate rituals shifting these...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T23:43:25-07:00","id":184592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/177987-bloodlines-and-blood-ties?p=184055#post184055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's also usual for childer to join their sire's bloodline and jumping around in non-family bloodlines is rarer. So that's why the definition holds. They are &quot;lineages&quot;, which may adopt children. Do adopted children count as full children? I wouldn't say so.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unlike adopted children, bloodline members feed from a member of the bloodline, and that changes them fundamentally. It would be as if you could shift someone's DNA when you adopted them. So it's not really a great comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T23:48:24-07:00","id":184615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/177987-bloodlines-and-blood-ties?p=184592#post184592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unlike adopted children, bloodline members feed from a member of the bloodline, and that changes them fundamentally. It would be as if you could shift someone's DNA when you adopted them. So it's not really a great comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha, was waiting for someone to call that one out on me. Anyways, while it's not a great comparison, it's the only one I know. In any case, as I said before, in my opinion, they are lineages not because their blood ties shift, but because it's usual for childes to join their sires. Adaption is a lot more rare in my opinion (just because requirements are higher, not even counting the fact that it's harder to prove yourself before a bloodline if you are not in the family tree already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T01:08:01-07:00","id":184651,"title":"","content":"Actually, 'adopting' someone allows an avus to be more picky. That person 'wants' to join the line, whereas someone embraced right into the line may end up not being a good fit. For instance, your childe, whom you carefully selected for the desired qualities you want in your bloodline is embraced straight into the line. They have a nervous breakdown after they accidentally kill their first human in a feeding frenzy and are usually either catatonic or extremely violent. Not only have they proven to be a disappointment with their inability to cope and adapt, but they decide to run out and embrace people into the line who decidedly don't fit the criteria you want for your line. While there is nothing that prevents that from being the case with someone inducted later, it's less likely to happen because their personalities have already been set and stabilized. They've typically weathered the traumatic experiences that make or break someone when they are first embraced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T05:34:06-08:00","id":834965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/177987-bloodlines-and-blood-ties?p=184651#post184651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, 'adopting' someone allows an avus to be more picky. That person 'wants' to join the line, whereas someone embraced right into the line may end up not being a good fit. For instance, your childe, whom you carefully selected for the desired qualities you want in your bloodline is embraced straight into the line. They have a nervous breakdown after they accidentally kill their first human in a feeding frenzy and are usually either catatonic or extremely violent. Not only have they proven to be a disappointment with their inability to cope and adapt, but they decide to run out and embrace people into the line who decidedly don't fit the criteria you want for your line. While there is nothing that prevents that from being the case with someone inducted later, it's less likely to happen because their personalities have already been set and stabilized. They've typically weathered the traumatic experiences that make or break someone when they are first embraced.</div> </div> </div> </div> case could be made that by joining a bloodline you leave your normal blood family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T12:59:40-08:00","id":835299,"title":"","content":"My thoughts on the matter. Your sire is your sire. Your blood sympathy will always be +3 that does not change. Your childe is always your childe. Your blood sympathy will always be +3. Your childe/sire grows and changes and decides to be part of a blood line... I feel like the developers would have stated in the book that you get blood sympathy at +something to your Avus. However they did not, which I feel is important to note. I would not give them blood sympathy at a + anything. The first line of blood sympathy is that the blood calls to blood. Because you have consumed 1 vitae from your &quot;mentor&quot; does not mean your blood is now his..<br /> <br /> However, they do note that you are susceptible to the Blood Bond and Addiction. Which gives you something like sympathy, but not quite... <br /> <br /> <br /> RAW: does not give an Avus sympathy. <br /> <br /> and everyone keeps saying adopting like you are adopting a childe ... I think it would be key to note that the developers use the word &quot;Mentor&quot;... not parent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T17:24:50-08:00","id":835477,"title":"","content":"How about members of the bloodline move up 1 step closer to each other for blood sympathy up to 2 steps removed. That way 1 step removed is still only for sire &amp; childe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10820,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","user":"Blakemikizuki","date":".  Rewording 02-22-2016, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T03:18:53-08:00","id":835662,"title":"","content":"That creates a lot of strange cases, of parts of family being bloodline, parts being not, and why would that change in normal families? It just... <br /> <br /> What's the point to have these blood ties there in the first place? I mean, what's wrong with having the bloodline adoption process leaving them as they are?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T05:26:43-08:00","id":835685,"title":"","content":"part of me says treat you and your avus as childe sire but it stops there.But his relations can feel him still including his reactions to you. Another part of me says 1) B&amp;S assumes clan ( and that can mean bloodline)is assumed to be related. 2. Your Avus did change the nature of your blood to become something else.<br /> <br /> I guess it depends on which I want emphasize. After all this is a tool kirt and I could see going both ways depending on my setting style sheet.<br /> <br /> In either case I seemed to be leaning on one should take precedent over the other. If you go with the latter then joining a bloodline has extra implications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T06:23:46-08:00","id":835705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/177987-bloodlines-and-blood-ties?p=835662#post835662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That creates a lot of strange cases, of parts of family being bloodline, parts being not, and why would that change in normal families? It just... <br /> <br /> What's the point to have these blood ties there in the first place? I mean, what's wrong with having the bloodline adoption process leaving them as they are?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because some bloodlines are open to more than one clan and if all bloodlines share blood sympathy even across different clans via then the concept of different clans is actually meaningless. (Or in the case of Harry Dresden and Red Court vampires very fatal.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T07:09:39-08:00","id":835740,"title":"","content":"Maybe not. If we take the interpretation of the clans as being 5 (or maybe just 4) completely separate types of monster that slowly drifted together to the point that they all identify as the same one then some cross-contamination of the sort caused by such a bloodline could explain it. Besides, the Coil of Voivode already lets a vampire establish a blood sympathy with anyone who tastes their blood. How is this any different?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T09:16:17-08:00","id":835823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/177987-bloodlines-and-blood-ties?p=835740#post835740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe not. If we take the interpretation of the clans as being 5 (or maybe just 4) completely separate types of monster that slowly drifted together to the point that they all identify as the same one then some cross-contamination of the sort caused by such a bloodline could explain it. Besides, the Coil of Voivode already lets a vampire establish a blood sympathy with anyone who tastes their blood. How is this any different?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> @ Elfive : it is different Because first you have to be in a covenant, be powerful enough to have that power, next have blood bonded someone enough times for them to get the sympathy.<br /> <br /> Neonate joeschmoe made last week who just happens to be in the bloodline that you want can be your Avus.. Your mentor .. Why would they suddenly have +3 to work mojo on you.. or +3 to feel your emotions?<br /> <br /> <br /> Are we just all ignoring the fact that an Avus is nothing more than a mentor and that the book does not give them any special powers?<br /> <br /> <br /> IF IF you say that your avus is suddenly your sire. Then I think you should take the humanity hit for creating a childe.<br /> Then what even happens to your other sire? What if you had created a childer? What happens to them? would there be a hole in the family tree? Then if you have a new sire, then your childe now has sympathy with them but does the old sire have sympathy with them too?<br /> <br /> Too many problems arise when you Make an Avus a new sire...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":".  clarification 02-23-2016, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T09:29:32-08:00","id":835832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/177987-bloodlines-and-blood-ties?p=835823#post835823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Because first you have to be in a covenant, be powerful enough to have that power, next have blood bonded someone enough times for them to get the sympathy.<br /> <br /> Neonate joeschmoe made last week who just happens to be in the bloodline that you want can be your Avus.. Your mentor .. Why would they suddenly have +3 to work mojo on you.. or +3 to feel your emotions?<br /> <br /> <br /> Are we just all ignoring the fact that an Avus is nothing more than a mentor and that the book does not give them any special powers?<br /> <br /> <br /> IF IF you say that your avus is suddenly your sire. Then I think you should take the humanity hit for creating a childe.<br /> Then what even happens to your other sire? What if you had created a childer? What happens to them? would there be a hole in the family tree? Then if you have a new sire, then your childe now has sympathy with them but does the old sire have sympathy with them too?<br /> <br /> Too many problems arise when you Make an Avus a new sire...</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless they changed the rules a blood bond is not required to join a bloodline AFAIK.<br /> Who can be your avus now depends how related you are and how powerful their blood is. <br /> Their blood changes yours and you gives blessings and weaknesses it did not have before.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T09:31:54-08:00","id":835837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/177987-bloodlines-and-blood-ties?p=835823#post835823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because first you have to be in a covenant, be powerful enough to have that power, next have blood bonded someone enough times for them to get the sympathy.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Irrelevant. Once you've established the bond there's no reason to treat the two cases any differently. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/177987-bloodlines-and-blood-ties?p=835823#post835823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neonate joeschmoe made last week who just happens to be in the bloodline that you want can be your Avus.. Your mentor .. Why would they suddenly have +3 to work mojo on you.. or +3 to feel your emotions?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Why <i>wouldn't </i>they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T09:35:57-08:00","id":835840,"title":"","content":"I was speaking to how the coil of the Voivode is different than an Avus. You are correct in saying a blood bond is not required though a potential risk.<br /> <br /> You have to have BP 4 to join through an Avus who is not related to you and BP 2 for someone who already shares a Sympathy. It does not say that the Avus is required to have any such BP.<br /> <br /> It does give you blessings and weaknesses which are both clearly stated, what is not stated that Your Avus becomes your New sire and therefore you get blood sympathy with them. It states they are your &quot;mentor&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Blood Bond and Blood Sympathy are two different ball games. Comparing apples and oranges there. <br /> <br /> as far as why they wouldnt.. is because the book does not state they become anything more than a mentor...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 02-23-2016, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T09:38:52-08:00","id":835842,"title":"","content":"Well, the way an avus works you're always going to have blood sympathy with them to some degree. It's just a question of whether or not it gets stronger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T09:40:21-08:00","id":835843,"title":"","content":"Where does it say that an Avus gives you blood Sympathy?<br /> <br /> Clarification: At any + to make it matter... Clan always has it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This whole thread's question and purpose was to clarify if an Avus became your new sire.. Unless we have deviated from that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 02-23-2016, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T22:51:47-08:00","id":836254,"title":"","content":"by RAW, it doesn't. There's no special connection, except for the two of you now being in the same bloodline, and probably with quite some story baggage (since you know, he had to do it somehow). <br /> <br /> Arguing for something which is not in the rules, in a thread meant to ask the question if it's in the rules is rather....<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, if one wanted to do a houserule, where he does increase the family step, he should answer all the questions posed in Vitalis' comment","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T04:31:42-08:00","id":836339,"title":"","content":"I do like the &quot;quality connection, different circuits&quot; interpretation. Connects the new bloodline member and the avus, but doesn't extend to either of their &quot;families&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T08:23:16-08:00","id":836418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/177987-bloodlines-and-blood-ties?p=836254#post836254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">by RAW, it doesn't. There's no special connection, except for the two of you now being in the same bloodline, and probably with quite some story baggage (since you know, he had to do it somehow).<br /> <br /> Arguing for something which is not in the rules, in a thread meant to ask the question if it's in the rules is rather....<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, if one wanted to do a houserule, where he does increase the family step, he should answer all the questions posed in Vitalis' comment</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I did make that assumption. But then again if a nos joins the mortrophians it kind of make sense there should be some connection. <br /> After all you are altering your blood and nature a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}